    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nConsolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into one derived **`identityKey`** = `normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`, where a new owner is rejected with **409** only when its *whole* key matches an existing owner's.\n\n### New code\n- **`util/IdentityKey.java`** \u2014 the single source of truth for the key. `of(Owner)` and `of(telephone, email, householdId)` join the three parts with `|`; a null/blank email or householdId becomes an empty segment. Both the create check and the response mapper derive the key here, so they agree. No re-normalization is needed: create steps normalize telephone/email before the check, and stored owners already hold the canonical values.\n- **`rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`** \u2014 the single duplicate step. Computes the candidate's key (resolving its prospective household id the same way `AssignHousehold` would) and compares it against every existing owner's key.\n- **`Households.resolveHouseholdId(...)`** \u2014 mirrors `AssignHousehold`'s decision so the candidate is compared against the id it would actually be assigned.\n- **`DuplicateIdentityException`** + handler + escalation YAML \u2192 409.\n\n### Wiring\n- `owners.POST.yml`: replaced `ensureUniqueEmail` \u2192 `ensureUniqueTelephone` \u2192 `ensureUniqueHousehold` with a single `ensureUniqueIdentity` step.\n\n### Response\n- Added `identityKey` (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`; `OwnerMapper` now derives it via `IdentityKey.of(owner)` (with `imports = IdentityKey.class` so the generated MapStruct impl compiles).\n\n### Removed (now dead)\n- `EnsureUniqueTelephone`, `EnsureUniqueEmail`, `EnsureUniqueHousehold`; the three `Duplicate{Telephone,Email,Household}Exception` classes + handlers + their escalation YAMLs. Fixed the stale Javadoc `@link` in `TelephoneNormalizer`.\n\n### Behaviour change (as specified)\nBecause telephone is part of the key, two same-household members (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are **both allowed** \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The provided acceptance test `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` (same telephone \u2192 409) passes, and `mvn test` is green.",
